$ whycant -u www-data delete /tmp/alice-session

✗ www-data (uid 33) cannot delete /tmp/alice-session

  /                    drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /tmp                 drwxrwxrwt  root:root    ✓ delete from
  /tmp/alice-session   -rw-------  alice:alice  ✗ delete   ← blocked here

Why
  /tmp has the sticky bit (the t in drwxrwxrwt), so only the file's owner (alice),
  the directory's owner (root) or root may delete or rename entries in it,
  even though www-data can write to the directory.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Ask alice, who owns the file, to delete it.
  2. Delete it as root:
       sudo rm -- /tmp/alice-session
